# The seasons on one tree through the year, with the weather each brings in Spain.
lesson language-seasons v=1 format=teach grade=4 unit=1 subject=language levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "The seasons"
  goal "Name the four seasons in [[language.name]] and say what the weather is like in each."

  look {
    scene 35x14 {
      column all at=canvas(1, 1) space=1 align=start {
        seasontrees trees seasons=["spring", "summer", "autumn", "winter"] names=1
      }
    }
    say """
      The year has four seasons: [[weather.spring]] (spring), [[weather.summer]] (summer),
      [[weather.autumn]] (autumn) and [[weather.winter]] (winter). In Spain summer is June, July and
      August, and it is hot: [[weather.in-summer-it-is-hot]]. In winter it is cold, and it snows in
      the mountains. In spring there are flowers, and in autumn the leaves fall.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked language.seasons-name k=4
    }
    show language.seasons-name k=2 easy-k=1 hard-k=5
    show language.seasons-meaning k=3 easy-k=2 hard-k=4
    show language.seasons-write k=3 easy-k=0
    show language.seasons-name k=4 easy-k=2 hard-k=6
    show language.seasons-match k=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2
    show language.seasons-write k=4 easy-k=3 hard-k=2
    show language.seasons-listen k=3 easy-k=0 hard-k=5
    show language.seasons-say k=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2
    level hard {
      show language.seasons-write k=1
    }
  }
  language es {
    try stars=2 {
      show language.es-seasons-why k=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2
    }
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show language.seasons-puzzle k=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2
  }
  remember {
    say "[[weather.spring|cap]], [[weather.summer]], [[weather.autumn]], [[weather.winter]]. [[weather.in-summer-it-is-hot|cap]]."
  }

  grown-ups """
    The wrong idea to watch for is that the seasons are the same everywhere, and autumn and winter
    swapped. The tree is the same tree drawn in each season, so the picture changes only in what a
    season changes. From this grade the written words are marked with their accents: a word typed
    without its accent is not taken. The dictation is read from this sheet, where it prints as Read
    aloud, or played by the device. If the child is stuck, sort the twelve months into four piles
    for the seasons. Off the page, look outside and say which season it is and one thing that shows
    it. It meets England's key stage 2 languages programme (years 3 to 6, statutory from age 7):
    "describe people, places, things and actions orally and in writing"; Japan's grades 5 and 6
    foreign languages: "Can talk about familiar and simple matters in daily life by using simple
    words and phrases and basic expressions"; and CEFR A1, "Can understand and use familiar everyday
    expressions and very basic phrases". The phrases are in [[language.variety]].
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level [[weather.in-summer-it-is-hot]] is worked first in the teacher's pen, the words to name are [[weather.winter]] and [[weather.spring]] and the words to write are [[weather.summer-word]] and [[weather.autumn-word]], the plainer ones of the lesson, with the first set to match, the shortest sentence to hear and the first version of each star question."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the words to name are [[weather.in-winter-it-snows]] and [[weather.in-spring-there-are-flowers]] and the words to write are [[weather.autumn-word]], [[weather.spring-word]] and [[weather.winter-word]], the ones most often mixed up, with the last set to match, the longest sentence to hear, a third word to write and the last version of each star question."
  }
}
